comment_regular_data.body:
@barrettruth This isn't AI slop, i wrote it myself. With all my PR's across all the repos i contribute to, I'm very open with my AI use. Neovim's one of the only ones I've gone out my way to write out the PR directly because you guys require so, and i use neovim myself (I usually stick to repo's that allow AI, but if I use something i tend to want to contribute). 
Is it the depth I write in? The only other time i write up things myself is when doing bug bounties, so the way i write always tends to be formal and indepth. Or was it because I referenced the exact failing jobs? For the record, yes I used AI tools to parse and search the log outputs to find the exact errors, but every word of this response was typed out by me. I'll assume that's the issue, but this is seriously a misunderstanding. 
Honestly, I even looked through other merged PR's to gauge at the amount of depth you guys tend to like your PR's written up in, since this isn't the first time. My last PR I wrote up myself (after being warned about AI use for the absolute first PR i wrote up), and this is the same. Sorry for responding back, I understand you guys get loads of slop, but being stopped from contributing in general irks me especially when I haven't actually done whats been accused of me.
